From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: allolive <160342668+allolive@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 17 Sep 2026 03:25:53 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] HevcSei: keep a long SEI payload type from wrapping

m_payloadType is accumulated in steps of 255 (one 0xFF byte per step)
but is a uint8_t, so a type written as FF 05 (260) wraps to 4 and is
read as a T.35 message. Widen it to uint32_t to match m_payloadSize.

The bounds checks this patch used to carry are not needed any more:
upstream 14bc737b0f "HevcSei: Stop at an SEI message that runs past the
NAL" compares the payload size against AvailableBits() / 8 and stops on
CBitstreamReader::Overflow(). That also covers the reason for the
AvailableBits() clamp this patch used to add: the only callers of
AvailableBits() are the two sites in HevcSei.cpp, and neither can reach
the wrapped value once Overflow() is checked.

Needs a malformed stream to trigger. Not exercised on hardware.

Signed-off-by: allolive <160342668+allolive@users.noreply.github.com>

diff --git a/xbmc/utils/HevcSei.h b/xbmc/utils/HevcSei.h
index b76d9e6..47a835b 100644
--- a/xbmc/utils/HevcSei.h
+++ b/xbmc/utils/HevcSei.h
@@ -30,7 +30,7 @@ public:
   CHevcSei() = default;
   ~CHevcSei() = default;
 
-  uint8_t m_payloadType{0};
+  uint32_t m_payloadType{0};
   size_t m_payloadSize{0};
 
   // In relation to the input SEI rbsp payload
